 question.","explanation":"Use there is with “a sign”: There is a sign beside the cycle lane.","keywords":[],"source":"seed","skill":"agreement","contextKey":"existence-50","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-there-is-there-are"],"version":"foundations-2026-09-v2","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"fingerprint":"9e7808448dc26c4dac30452de3a49b8147ecae3ef1015e5618d9b50094607ff4","teaching":{"steps":["Identify what the question tests: **agreement**. Use there is before a singular or uncountable noun. Use there are before a plural noun. These exercises use standard written agreement.","Use there is with “a sign”: There is a sign beside the cycle lane.","Choose **is**. Check the completed expression against the subject, time and intended meaning in the prompt."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Use there is with “a sign”: There is a sign beside the cycle lane.","B":"**are** does not match the subject’s person/number or the construction’s tense here. Use there is with “a sign”: There is a sign beside the cycle lane.","C":"Base **be** does not supply the finite agreement required here. Use there is with “a sign”: There is a sign beside the cycle lane.","D":"**am** does not match the subject’s person/number or the construction’s tense here. Use there is with “a sign”: There is a sign beside the cycle lane."}}},{"id":"2700d316-f7c1-5b94-a399-fcc480bc72d3","topicSlug":"there-is-there-are","level":"A1","prompt":"Use the negative form of there is: There ____ a sign beside the cycle lane.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"are not"},{"id":"B","text":"do not"},{"id":"C","text":"not be"},{"id":"D","text":"is not"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Put is or are before there to ask a question. Put not after the verb to make a negative. Focus on **negative** in this question.","explanation":"Place not after is; retain its agreement with “a sign”.","keywords":[],"source":"seed","skill":"negative","contextKey":"existence-50","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-there-is-there-are"],"version":"foundations-2026-09-v2","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"fingerprint":"26aee1b628cf5430a5c24c7b4c2dc3c1f0fcbe840fb22eac2345e2a665b38014","teaching":{"steps":["Identify what the question tests: **negative**. Put is or are before there to ask a question. Put not after the verb to make a negative.","Place not after is; retain its agreement with “a sign”.","Choose **is not**. Check the completed expression against the subject, time and intended meaning in the prompt."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**are** does not match the subject’s person/number or the construction’s tense here. Place not after is; retain its agreement with “a sign”.","B":"This construction uses its existing **is** form, so **do not** introduces the wrong auxiliary. Place not after is; retain its agreement with “a sign”.","C":"Base **be** does not supply the finite agreement required here. Place not after is; retain its agreement with “a sign”.","D":"Place not after is; retain its agreement with “a sign”."}}},{"id":"21c9c439-0efd-585c-afa3-9a2bc0822d92","topicSlug":"there-is-there-are","level":"A1","prompt":"____ there a sign beside the cycle lane? Ask whether it exists now.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Has"},{"id":"B","text":"Is"},{"id":"C","text":"Are"},{"id":"D","text":"Does"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Put is or are before there to ask a question. Put not after the verb to make a negative. Focus on **question** in this question.","explanation":"Put is before there: Is there a sign beside the cycle lane?","keywords":[],"source":"seed","skill":"question","contextKey":"existence-50","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-there-is-there-are"],"version":"foundations-2026-09-v2","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"fingerprint":"e90cd94013bba18e867c6285c8aa1653f88f2f5993dec2bbf6714d466d3ac130","teaching":{"steps":["Identify what the question tests: **question**. Put is or are before there to ask a question. Put not after the verb to make a negative.","Put is before there: Is there a sign beside the cycle lane?","Choose **Is**. Check the completed expression against the subject, time and intended meaning in the prompt."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**has** does not match the subject’s person/number or the construction’s tense here. Put is before there: Is there a sign beside the cycle lane?","B":"Put is before there: Is there a sign beside the cycle lane?","C":"**are** does not match the subject’s person/number or the construction’s tense here. Put is before there: Is there a sign beside the cycle lane?","D":"This construction uses its existing **is** form, so **Does** introduces the wrong auxiliary. Put is before there: Is there a sign beside the cycle lane?"}}},{"id":"eeea16ec-7252-5278-a363-edea4527be3d","topicSlug":"there-is-there-are","level":"A1","prompt":"“Is there a sign beside the cycle lane?” Complete the positive short answer: “Yes, there ____.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"has"},{"id":"B","text":"be"},{"id":"C","text":"is"},{"id":"D","text":"are"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Keep there and the matching verb in a short answer. In a positive answer, do not shorten there is to there’s. Focus on **short answer** in this question.","explanation":"The short answer keeps there is. A positive there is answer keeps the full verb.","keywords":[],"source":"seed","skill":"short-answer","contextKey":"existence-50","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-there-is-there-are"],"version":"foundations-2026-09-v2","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"fingerprint":"6a943bf9bbba285c9eed724d9621bf395971dd85f3b57f11c1d42f7efb3eb3ba","teaching":{"steps":["Identify what the question tests: **short answer**. Keep there and the matching verb in a short answer. In a positive answer, do not shorten there is to there’s.","The short answer keeps there is. A positive there is answer keeps the full verb.","Choose **is**. Check the completed expression against the subject, time and intended meaning in the prompt."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**has** does not match the subject’s person/number or the construction’s tense here. The short answer keeps there is. A positive there is answer keeps the full verb.","B":"Base **be** does not supply the finite agreement required here. The short answer keeps there is. A positive there is answer keeps the full verb.","C":"The short answer keeps there is. A positive there is answer keeps the full verb.","D":"**are** does not match the subject’s person/number or the construction’s tense here. The short answer keeps there is. A positive there is answer keeps the full verb."}}}],"chapter":{"introduction":["Existential there introduces the presence of something. It lets a new thing enter the conversation naturally: There is a café nearby. This differs from The café is nearby, which starts from an already identified café. The verb reflects the number or amount introduced."],"rules":[{"title":"Existence and number","explanation":"Use there is before a singular or uncountable noun. Use there are before a plural noun. These exercises use standard written agreement.","examples":["There is a light above the gate.","There are two seats near the exit.","There **is** a clock above the door."],"pattern":"There **is** a seat / There **are** two seats","paragraphs":["Use there is with a singular count noun or an uncountable amount. Use there are with plural count nouns. In There is some equipment, equipment is uncountable and takes singular agreement even if it includes many separate objects."]},{"title":"Questions and negatives","explanation":"Put is or are before there to ask a question. Put not after the verb to make a negative.","examples":["Is there a bicycle stand?","There are not any spare chairs.","There **are not** any spare tickets."],"pattern":"**Is there** a seat? / There **is not** a seat.","paragraphs":["Move is or are before there in a question. Put not after it in a negative. Any is common before a plural or uncountable noun in open questions and negatives: Are there any chairs? There isn’t any water."]},{"title":"Short answers","explanation":"Keep there and the matching verb in a short answer. In a positive answer, do not shorten there is to there’s.","examples":["Yes, there is.","No, there are not.","**Is there** enough time? — Yes, there **is**."],"pattern":"Yes, there **is**. / No, there **is not**.","paragraphs":["A short answer keeps there and the auxiliary: Yes, there are. The positive short answer does not normally end in a contraction such as Yes, there’s. Here there is a grammatical subject, not a location meaning over there."]},{"title":"Contrasts and edge cases","explanation":"Informal speech sometimes uses there’s before a list or plural, but these exercises practise standard written number agreement. Other tenses are possible: there was, there were, there will be and there has been. Distinguish there, their and they’re: they have different grammatical jobs.","examples":["There **is** a clock above the door.","There **are not** any spare tickets.","**Is there** enough time? — Yes, there **is**."]}],"recap":["There **is** a seat / There **are** two seats","**Is there** a seat? / There **is not** a seat.","Yes, there **is**. / No, there **is not**."]},"stage":"1 · Sentence foundations","prerequisites":["possessive-s"]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT(version,slug) DO NOTHING;
